  "publisher": "Initiative",
  "description": "Native, First Nations, and still here.",
  "long_description": "For Native and Indigenous groups and the relatives who stand with them. Stepped weaving, an eight-pointed star quilt, Northwest Coast formline, painted parfleche, pottery banding and Woodlands floral beadwork for banners; the four directions round your picture; and trophies for the red handprint, an eagle feather and the medicine wheel. Two-Spirit gets its own banner and trophy: two feathers bound at the quill, hanging over the six colours. Every design here is original work in the tradition's own structure — no crest, no seal, and no nation's, family's or weaver's own pattern.",
